        {
          "role": "statement",
          "basis": "source",
          "text": "The term λx. x (x (x x)) is a lambda abstraction whose body applies the bound variable x to the result of applying x to (x x).",
          "requires": [],
          "citationRequired": false
        },
        {
          "role": "derivation",
          "basis": "source",
          "text": "Applying this abstraction to N substitutes N for every occurrence of the bound variable x in its body, yielding N (N (N N)) by beta-reduction.",
          "requires": [],
          "citationRequired": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
